# ZMODEM Transfer Demo
# Pull a file from the demo device, push it back under a new name, and
# do a batch pull. The device runs the same ZMODEM engine a real board
# would, so every transfer is a genuine round trip.

/print ─── ZMODEM Transfer Demo ───

/print
/print [1] What the device has to offer
AT+FS.LIST
/delay 300ms

/print
/print [2] Pull firmware_v1.bin from the device (device sends, we receive)
AT+ZMODEM=SEND firmware_v1.bin
/xfer.zmodem.recv
/delay 300ms

/print
/print [3] Show what landed in cap/
/cap.list
/delay 300ms

/print
/print [4] Push it back to the device under a new name (we send, device receives)
AT+ZMODEM=RECV
/xfer.zmodem.send firmware_v1.bin
/delay 300ms

/print
/print [5] Confirm the device now holds it
AT+FS.LIST
/delay 300ms

/print
/print [6] Batch pull: grab every file on the device at once
AT+ZMODEM=SEND
/xfer.zmodem.recv
/delay 300ms
/cap.list

/print
/print ─── Demo complete ───
